## Request Type
New Feature

## 👤 User Story
As a security engineer, I want automatic refresh token rotation with revocation detection so that stolen tokens are quickly invalidated and security breaches are contained.

## 🚨 Problem Statement, Use Case, or Opportunity
JWT refresh tokens are long-lived credentials that require special handling:

**Security Risks:**
- Stolen refresh tokens grant indefinite access
- No detection of token reuse attacks
- Compromised tokens remain valid until expiration
- No mechanism for immediate revocation
- Replay attacks possible

**Attack Scenarios:**
- XSS attack steals refresh token from storage
- Network interception captures token
- Malware extracts tokens from browser
- Token leaked in logs or error messages
- Database breach exposes tokens

## 💡 Proposed Solution
Implement RFC 6819 compliant refresh token rotation:

**Token Rotation Strategy:**
1. Each refresh generates new access + refresh token pair
2. Old refresh token immediately invalidated
3. Old token stored in database (revoked status)
4. Reuse detection: if revoked token used, revoke entire token family
5. Token family tracking via lineage

**Implementation:**
```csharp
public class RefreshTokenCommand
{
    public string RefreshToken { get; set; }
}

public class RefreshTokenResult
{
    public string AccessToken { get; set; }
    public string RefreshToken { get; set; }
    public DateTime ExpiresAt { get; set; }
}

public class RefreshToken
{
    public Guid Id { get; set; }
    public string Token { get; set; }
    public Guid UserId { get; set; }
    public Guid? ParentTokenId { get; set; } // Token lineage
    public Guid SessionId { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
    public DateTime ExpiresAt { get; set; }
    public DateTime? RevokedAt { get; set; }
    public string RevokedByIp { get; set; }
    public string ReplacedByToken { get; set; }
    public bool IsRevoked => RevokedAt != null;
    public bool IsExpired => DateTime.UtcNow >= ExpiresAt;
    public bool IsActive => !IsRevoked && !IsExpired;
}
```

**Reuse Detection:**
```csharp
public async Task<TokenResult> RefreshAsync(string token)
{
    var refreshToken = await GetRefreshTokenAsync(token);

    // If token already used (replaced), it's a reuse attack
    if (refreshToken.ReplacedByToken != null)
    {
        // Revoke entire token family
        await RevokeTokenFamilyAsync(refreshToken);

        // Alert security team
        await SendSecurityAlertAsync(refreshToken.UserId, 
            "Refresh token reuse detected");

        throw new SecurityException("Token reuse detected");
    }

    if (!refreshToken.IsActive)
        throw new InvalidTokenException();

    // Generate new token pair
    var newTokens = await GenerateTokenPairAsync(refreshToken.UserId);

    // Mark old token as replaced
    refreshToken.RevokedAt = DateTime.UtcNow;
    refreshToken.ReplacedByToken = newTokens.RefreshToken;

    await SaveAsync();

    return newTokens;
}
```

**Token Revocation:**
```csharp
public class RevokeTokenCommand
{
    public string RefreshToken { get; set; }
    public string Reason { get; set; }
}

// Revoke specific token
await RevokeTokenAsync(token);

// Revoke all user tokens (force re-login)
await RevokeAllUserTokensAsync(userId);

// Revoke token family (security breach)
await RevokeTokenFamilyAsync(tokenId);
```

